{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Fund NHS clinical trials of psilocybin-assisted therapy",
        "additional_details": "Many people with treatment-resistant depression, PTSD and other serious mental health conditions do not recover with current treatments. UK research at King\u2019s College London and Imperial College is already studying psychedelic-assisted therapy. NHS-backed trials could test safety, benefits, risks and long-term outcomes in a legal, regulated healthcare setting, and help guide future UK mental health policy.",
        "background": "Fund and support NHS-backed clinical trials of psychedelic-assisted therapy for treatment-resistant mental illness, with approved research sites, licensed clinicians, safety screening, psychological support, patient follow-up, and published evidence to guide future UK policy.",
